<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Kantakouzenos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1326–<a href="/years/1380">1380</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Kantakouzenos was the first despot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a>, the Byzantine province in the Peloponnese, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mystras">Mystras</a> from 1349 to 1380. Appointed by his father, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a>, he gave the province a permanent ruler, restored order among its quarrelling landowners and defended it against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> and Turkish raids.</p></div>
